(a) Applicants for a short-term vacation rental certificate must submit, on an annual basis, an application for a short-term vacation rental certificate to City Hall in the City of Rossville. The application must be furnished under oath on a form specified by the city clerk and accompanied by a non-refundable application fee in the amount of $25.00. The application must include:
(1) The address of the unit to be used as a short-term vacation rental;
(2) The name, address, telephone number, and email address of the owner(s) of record of the dwelling unit for which a certificate is sought. If such owner is not a natural person, the application must identify all members, partners, officers, or directors of any such entity, including personal contact information;
(3) The name, address, telephone number, and email address of the short-term vacation rental agent, which shall constitute their 24-hour contact information;
(4) The owner's sworn acknowledgement that they have received a copy of this section, have reviewed it and understand its requirements;
(5) An acknowledgement that parking spaces are not allowed on the grass or in the road;
(6) The owner's agreement to use his or her best efforts to ensure that use of the premises by short-term vacation rental occupants will not disrupt the neighborhood and will not interfere with the rights of neighboring property owners to the quiet enjoyment of their properties;
(7) Any other relevant information as determined by the city clerk or their designee which is necessary to achieve the objectives of this article;
(b) Along with the application, the applicant must attach the following:
(1) An owner's affidavit;
(2) A written rental agreement, which consists of the form of document to be executed between the owner and occupant(s), which must contain the following provisions and which must be posted in the short-term vacation rental unit:
a. The occupant(s)' agreement to abide by all of the requirements of this article, all other City of Rossville ordinances, state and federal law, and acknowledgement that their rights under the agreement may not be transferred or assigned to anyone else.
b. The occupant(s)' acknowledgement that it is unlawful to allow or make any noise or sound that exceeds the limits set forth in the city's noise ordinance.
c. The occupant(s)' acknowledgement and agreement that violation of the agreement or the provisions of this article may result in immediate termination of the agreement and eviction from the short-term vacation rental unit by the owner or agent, as well as the potential liability for payments of fines levied by the city; and.
d. The occupant(s)' acknowledgement on the maximum occupancy, based on number of beds, of the short-term vacation rental unit and, if available, the location of on-site parking.
(3) Proof of the owner's current ownership of the subject dwelling unit;
(4) Proof of insurance indicating the premises is used as a short-term vacation rental;
(5) A written certification from the short-term vacation agent that they agree to perform the duties applicable to their position as a short-term vacation rental agent as provided by this article.
